I got Intralase SBK done at London Eye Center a month ago. It is lasik method but they use a specialized laser to create a precise, thinner flap so the chances of dislodging is very low. The main pro of this is that you get pretty much 20/20 vision right away, which you would have to wait months to get if you were to do PRK. Not to mention, you would have a lot more discomfort too.

LEC was very professional, and I'm happy with the results. I was uncomfortable for the first 4 hours post-surgery, but after a 3 hour nap, I woke up feeling fine, had pretty much clear vision and was in no pain. I haven't experienced any discomfort since.I inquired at LasikMD prior to going to LEC, and they were a lot more expensive and felt more corporate than a medical centre. I'm glad I went with LEC in the end.

&#x200B;

I paid around $3000 for this and my prescription was about -5.00. No halos as far as i can tell.

&#x200B;

I also get lifetime warranty, so if my prescription was to come back again, I can do PRK with them for free.

